[Music]  okay i'm gonna spend the next five  minutes talking about the most overrated  productivity hack on the internet in my  opinion which is the pomodoro method you  might have used this technique  effectively in the past i certainly have  but i now have come to the point where  i've found that in the long term it  turns out to be a lot worse for my  productivity and work so in this video  i'm going to talk about three main  reasons why i personally think that this  technique might not be as good as we  think it is very briefly the pomodoro  technique is a study or work method  where you work for a set period of time  usually 20 minutes and then you take a  five minute break and you repeat this  again and again now the first reason  that i hate it is because it tends to be  the anti-flow method of productivity a  flow state is a state where we are 100  enthralled in what we are doing we have  lost perhaps all sense of time and space  and we are focusing purely on what we  are doing at the time the state has been  described by many psychologists and it  tends to feel deeply deeply fun and  engaging however it takes a lot of time  to get to this point usually a lot more  than 20 minutes so if we are limiting  ourselves by working for only 20 minutes  at a time we can essentially never reach  flow and even if we somehow tend to  reach flow very early on we will be  interrupted and stopped as being called  out of the state by a huge distraction  like a timer for a break means that then  we kind of lose our sense of working  very hard on something and then go back  to baseline of being distracted and  perhaps taking a lot more work to get  back into the mindset of working in  general so even though i don't reach the  flow state every single time that i am  studying or working in general i do like  to think that i have the option to do it  and it's much more likely that i do it  if i don't have a timer to stop at some  point the second reason i usually  dislike the pomodoro method is because  it creates a dichotomy between working  and taking a break and this is hugely  problematic if we create this  distinction then we are saying that work  is in a way a thing that is bad or a  thing that we don't enjoy or a thing  that we have to do and rest is something  that we like a thing that we enjoy and a  thing that we want to do and even though  most of us would agree that this is  actually the state well if we know that  we have to do work we might as well  enjoy it there are some very interesting  studies that were done with children  wherein two groups were given tasks to  do one group was rewarded for the task  and one group wasn't the children who  were rewarded for the task in the long  term ended up not enjoying it and the  ones who weren't rewarded were just made  to do it with nothing good given to them  after ended up enjoying the task a lot  more and the reasoning that the  psychologists gave for this experiment  was that when children are rewarded for  doing something their brains start to  think oh i must not enjoy this task  because i am being paid to do it it must  be something that i don't want to do  well when they are not given a reward  the brain justifies this by thinking oh  this must be something that i enjoy  doing it because i'm doing it for no  reason or for no reward and therefore  they end up liking this activity much  more in the long term this kind of goes  against our theory of positive  reinforcement for things but this is  something that has been well documented  in child growth so for this reason i try  to apply the same method to myself where  i very often stop rewarding myself for  doing things i don't want to do and in  the long term i end up enjoying those  things more counterintuitively so with  the pomodoro technique because you are  rewarding yourself with a break or with  food or whatever you want to do or enjoy  in that five minute break then it makes  you subconsciously feel as though the  work is something that you have to do  and you really don't want to and you  really don't enjoy rather than just  forcing yourself to do the work with no  reward which will then make you think  that oh i must enjoy this thing that i  keep on doing for no reason third and  last reason that i deeply don't enjoy  the pomodoro method is that whenever i  put a timer be that a timer just for  food or a timer for working or a timer  for studying there's a part of my brain  that is paying attention to the timer  constantly a part of my brain which is  waiting for that kind of signal and that  alarm to go off and no matter what i  cannot focus 100 on what i am doing  because a part of my attention will  constantly be distracted on my phone or  on a kind of timer device that i might  have somewhere and i really don't like  this split brain thinking because then i  tend to be a lot less productive in the  task that i am actually doing if you're  constantly calculating oh it might be 10  minutes to go or oh i think i might be  halfway or surely can't be more than two  minutes left that's not a very  productive place to be so i'm almost  running out of time so i do need to wrap  this video up but this was my reasoning  as to why i don't like the pomodoro  technique and if you made it so far  thank you so much for spending this time  with me i hope you have a wonderful rest  of your day be kind yourself and others  and don't believe everything you think  thanks bye  [Music]

